For those looking to book an experience or plan a birthday party with us, we have several important links available. You can make general bookings through this URL: https://ecom.roller.app/aerosportsscarborough/products/en/home. If you're planning a birthday celebration, please use our dedicated booking page at https://ecom.roller.app/aerosportsscarborough/birthdayparties/en/products. For safety and compliance purposes, waivers are required for all participants; these can be accessed and completed online at https://waiver.roller.app/aerosportsscarborough/. If you need directions to our location, we have a Google Maps link available here: https://g.page/AeroSports-scarborough. Lastly, if you're planning a birthday party with us, you might find it helpful to send out invitations through this link: https://aerosportsinvitation.netlify.app/invitationscarborough.

If there's anything else you need or any other questions you have about visiting AeroSports Scarborough, feel free to ask!

[4] (source: chatbot_quick_replies.md)
At AeroSports Scarborough, you can enjoy a wide range of activities designed to suit all ages and preferences. Our offerings include wall-to-wall trampolines, a ninja warrior course, ninja maze, rock climbing walls, dodgeball, slam basketball, a 360 bicycle ride, giant slides, a jump tower, and go-karting. Most of these attractions are included in your jump pass, with the exception of go-karting.

When it comes to pricing, we offer several options for our jump passes. A ninety-minute Premium Jump Pass costs twenty-four dollars and ninety cents, while a one hundred and twenty-minute VIP Jump Pass is priced at twenty-nine dollars and ninety cents. For those looking to enjoy all day, the All Day Pass is available for thirty-nine dollars and ninety cents. Please note that AeroSports grip socks are required for trampoline activities and cost three dollars and ninety-nine cents; however, they are reusable. Keep in mind that all prices include tax. Go-karting is a separate activity with pricing starting at nine dollars and ninety cents. Would you like to proceed with booking?

Our facility welcomes guests of all ages! Children as young as those who can walk are welcome to join the fun. For our youngest visitors, children under two years old can enter for free when accompanied by a paying adult. Additionally, we offer Toddler Time on Saturday mornings from nine to ten ante meridiem exclusively for children aged five and under at fifteen dollars and ninety cents per child, with one parent allowed to jump for free.

If you're considering celebrating a birthday with us, we have three exciting packages starting at thirty-nine dollars and ninety cents per jumper, with a minimum requirement of ten kids. Each package includes pizza, drinks, access to a private party room, a glow t-shirt for the birthday child, and digital invitations. The Ultimate Package goes above and beyond by including go-karting, a free thirty-day pass, and complimentary socks for everyone attending. Would you like more details on a specific package?

For those wondering about our location, AeroSports Scarborough is situated at one thousand one hundred and twenty Birchmount Road in Scarborough, Ontario, M1K 5G4. You can easily find us using Google Maps by searching for AeroSports Scarborough. If you need to reach us directly, our phone number is two-eight-nine-four-five-four-five-five-five-five.

Safety is a top priority at AeroSports Scarborough. We ensure the well-being of all our guests with trained staff and clearly posted park rules throughout the facility. Our trampolines have a weight limit of three hundred pounds for safety reasons. All jumpers are required to have a signed waiver, and children under ten years old must be accompanied by an adult. Spectators can enjoy the activities free of charge and we provide comfortable seating along with complimentary Wi-Fi for parents.

If you have any more questions or need further assistance, feel free to ask!

[5] (source: passes.md)
At AeroSports Scarborough, we offer a variety of passes that cater to different visiting preferences and needs. Whether you're planning a single day's adventure or looking for long-term access, our pass options are designed to suit everyone from occasional visitors to frequent jumpers.

The All Day Pass is perfect if you want to enjoy unlimited trampoline time in just one visit. It costs thirty-nine dollars and ninety cents and remains valid until the end of the day on which it's purchased. This pass allows you to jump all day long, making it ideal for those who wish to make the most out of a single day at our facility.

For those looking to spread their visits over a month, we offer the 30 Day Pass. Priced at forty-nine dollars and ninety cents plus tax, this pass is valid for thirty days from the date of purchase. Each visit under this pass grants you sixty minutes of jump time, allowing you to enjoy our trampolines multiple times within that period.

If you're planning more frequent visits over a longer span, consider our 90 Day Pass. This option costs one hundred and forty-nine dollars and ninety cents plus tax and is valid for ninety days from the purchase date. Similar to the 30 Day Pass, it provides sixty minutes of jump time per visit, giving you ample opportunity to enjoy our facilities throughout the three months.

For those who love jumping at AeroSports Scarborough and want year-round access, we have the Annual Pass. This pass costs three hundred and sixty-four dollars and ninety cents plus tax and is valid for three hundred and sixty-five days from purchase. Like the other passes, it offers sixty minutes of jump time per visit, ensuring you can enjoy our trampolines throughout the entire year.

Each pass provides a different level of access and duration to suit your lifestyle and visiting frequency, all while offering great value for those who love jumping at AeroSports Scarborough. If you have any questions about which pass might be best for you or need assistance with purchasing, feel free to ask!

[6] (source: attractions.md)
Welcome to AeroSports Scarborough! We offer a wide range of attractions suitable for all ages, ensuring there's something fun and exciting for everyone. Whether you're looking for thrilling rides, challenging obstacle courses, or energetic team games, we've got it covered. Many of our activities are included with any jump pass, making it easy for families to enjoy multiple attractions without additional costs.

Our Freestyle/Open Jump area features wall-to-wall trampolines where guests can jump, flip, and freestyle. This main trampoline area is interconnected, allowing for endless bouncing fun. It's suitable for all ages—any child who can walk can join in the fun. The cost of jumping here is included with any jump pass you purchase.

Next up are our Rock Walls, which offer indoor rock climbing at various difficulty levels. Guests can test their strength and push their limits as they climb to the top. Like the trampolines, these walls are open to all ages, and the activity is also included in any jump pass pricing.

For those who love racing, we have Indoor Go Karting on two tracks: a Main Track for taller riders and a Mini Track for younger kids. The karts are electric, allowing up to ten laps per race. To ride on the Main Track, participants must be at least fifty-two inches tall, while the Mini Track requires riders to be at least thirty-six inches tall. Both tracks require closed-toed shoes. Go Karting is not included in any jump pass and has separate ticket pricing.

Our 360 Bicycle attraction offers a pedal-powered thrill ride where you cycle through a full three hundred sixty-degree loop in the air, providing an experience unique to our park. This ride is open to all ages and is included with any jump pass.

For high-speed sliding fun, we have the Donut Slide and Carpet Slide. Guests can grab a tube or carpet and race down these giant slides, making it great for all ages. These slides are also included in any jump pass pricing.

The Dodgeball arena features trampoline dodgeball where you can bounce and throw in an energetic team game setting. This high-energy activity is perfect for groups looking for competitive fun and is included with any jump pass.

Slam Basketball or Aero Slam lets guests experience trampoline basketball hoops, allowing them to bounce and dunk like a pro. This attraction is suitable for all ages and comes at no additional cost when you have a jump pass.

Our Ninja Maze offers an obstacle course maze filled with twists, turns, and challenges designed to test your agility and ninja skills. It's open to all ages and included in any jump pass pricing.

For thrill seekers, the Jump Tower or Aero Drop provides an adrenaline-filled free-fall jump from above. Guests can leap off the tower and land safely below, making it a great attraction for those seeking excitement. This is also included with any jump pass.

The Ninja Warrior course is a full obstacle challenge inspired by the popular TV show, testing your strength, speed, and agility. It's suitable for all skill levels and ages, and like many of our attractions, it’s included in any jump pass pricing.

Our Laser Tag arena offers high-energy gameplay featuring immersive lighting, sound effects, and tactical team competition. This attraction is designed for fast-paced action and is suitable for all ages but requires a separate ticket or add-on purchase as it's not included with the jump pass.

Lastly, we have Bazooka Ball—an action-packed arena where players use air-powered launchers to shoot soft foam balls at targets and opponents. Like Laser Tag, this attraction is open to all ages but requires a separate ticket or add-on since it’s not part of any jump pass package.

We hope you enjoy your visit to AeroSports Scarborough! If you have any questions about our attractions or need assistance with booking, feel free to ask.

[7] (source: birthday_parties.md)
At AeroSports Scarborough, we offer three distinct birthday party packages: Premium, VIP, and Ultimate. Each package caters to groups of at least ten jumpers and includes a variety of amenities such as pizza, drinks, a private party room, a glow t-shirt, digital invitations, and a free sixty-minute add-on pass for guest jumpers.

The Premium Party is priced at thirty-nine dollars and ninety cents per jumper. This package requires a minimum of ten jumpers with a base price of three hundred and ninety-nine dollars. It includes seventy-five minutes on the trampoline courts followed by forty-five minutes in a private party room, which accommodates twenty-five to thirty people. Food included consists of one large pizza for every five jumpers and one juice box per jumper. The birthday child receives a free glow t-shirt, digital invitations, and a free sixty-minute jump pass, while all guest jumpers get a free sixty-minute add-on pass. Go karting is not included but can be added on at nine dollars and ninety cents per person. There are no discounts for socks, no physical invitations provided, and bringing outside food incurs a fifty-dollar fee. The total party duration is approximately two hours.

The VIP Party costs forty-four dollars and ninety cents per jumper with the same minimum requirement of ten jumpers and a base price of four hundred and forty-nine dollars. This package offers ninety minutes on the trampoline courts followed by sixty minutes in a private party room, also accommodating twenty-five to thirty people. Food includes one large pizza for every five jumpers, plus one juice box and one water bottle per jumper. The birthday child receives a free glow t-shirt, digital invitations, and a free sixty-minute jump pass, while all guest jumpers receive a free sixty-minute add-on pass. Socks are available at fifty percent off, costing two dollars instead of three dollars and ninety-nine cents. Go karting can be added on for nine dollars and ninety cents per person, with no physical invitations included, and outside food requires a fifty-dollar fee. The total party duration is approximately two and a half hours.

The Ultimate Party is priced at fifty-nine dollars and ninety cents per jumper, also requiring a minimum of ten jumpers with a base price of five hundred and ninety-nine dollars. This package includes one hundred and twenty minutes on the trampoline courts followed by sixty minutes in a private party room for twenty-five to thirty people. Food consists of one large pizza for every five jumpers, plus one juice box or pop and one water bottle per jumper. The birthday child receives a free glow t-shirt, digital and physical invitations, and a free thirty-day jump pass. All guest jumpers receive a free sixty-minute add-on pass. Socks are provided for free to all jumpers, and go karting is included with one race per jumper. The fifty-dollar outside food fee is waived. The total party duration is approximately three hours.

When upgrading from the Premium Party to the VIP Party, you gain an additional fifteen minutes of jump time (ninety versus seventy-five), fifteen more minutes in the private room (sixty versus forty-five), a water bottle along with the juice box, and socks at fifty percent off (two dollars instead of three dollars and ninety-nine cents). The cost difference is five dollars per jumper, which amounts to fifty dollars for ten jumpers.

Upgrading from the VIP Party to the Ultimate Party adds thirty more minutes of jump time (one hundred and twenty versus ninety), includes go karting for every jumper, provides free socks for all jumpers, offers physical invitations, gives a birthday child a free thirty-day pass instead of sixty minutes, waives the fifty-dollar outside food fee, and allows drinks to include pop as an option. The cost difference is fifteen dollars per jumper, totaling one hundred and fifty dollars for ten jumpers.

The Ultimate Party offers the best value with go karting alone worth nine dollars and ninety cents per jumper (ninety-nine dollars for ten kids), free socks valued at three dollars and ninety-nine cents each (thirty-nine dollars and ninety cents for ten), and a waived fifty-dollar outside food fee. This equates to roughly one hundred and eighty-nine dollars in extras for one hundred and fifty dollars more than the VIP Party.


